1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,004
Your health insurance claim was denied. That is not the final answer. This is ClaimSaathi.

2
00:00:08,719 --> 00:00:26,291
In a single year, twenty six thousand crore rupees of health claims were denied. Thirty six lakh claims were rejected outright. Yet fewer than one in a hundred ever reach the Insurance Ombudsman, even though more than half of the cases the Ombudsman decides end in the policyholder's favour or a settlement.

3
00:00:26,869 --> 00:00:37,454
Families give up because denial letters quote clauses nobody understands, decisions land at the discharge desk, and their rights stay invisible. ClaimSaathi flips that.

4
00:00:38,490 --> 00:00:47,541
Let's see it live. Meet Ramesh. His angioplasty claim of one point eight four lakh rupees was rejected for not disclosing hypertension.

5
00:00:47,541 --> 00:00:57,204
One click. ClaimSaathi parses the letter, finds the clause the insurer cited, and runs six tests from IRDAI's 2024 Master Circular.

6
00:00:57,204 --> 00:01:13,164
Verdict: strong case. Ramesh has been covered for sixty three months. After sixty months, IRDAI's moratorium rule says non-disclosure cannot be raised unless there is proven fraud. And the thirty six month pre-existing disease wait was served long ago.

7
00:01:13,165 --> 00:01:21,905
Every finding is backed by a quoted line. Here is the clause the insurer cited, and the moratorium clause in his own policy that defeats it.

8
00:01:21,905 --> 00:01:34,356
Then a dated escalation plan, and ready to send drafts. A grievance to the insurer, the Bima Bharosa complaint, and an Ombudsman filing, each citing the exact rule. Copy, or download.

9
00:01:34,356 --> 00:01:47,518
Case two. A cataract claim denied under a forty eight month waiting period. IRDAI caps every waiting period at thirty six months. And the discharge decision took five and a half hours, against a three hour limit.

10
00:01:47,518 --> 00:01:57,821
And when a denial is sound, ClaimSaathi says so honestly, then tells the family what evidence could still change the outcome, like a medical necessity certificate.

11
00:01:58,626 --> 00:02:13,222
Feature tour. PDF and photo ingest. Clause retrieval. Six rule tests. A strength verdict. Quote or abstain evidence. Three legal drafts. A dated escalation plan. Private by design, and mobile ready.

12
00:02:13,821 --> 00:02:28,656
Under the hood: clause aware parsing, retrieval, deterministic rule tests written as code, explanations with quoted evidence, and action. Next on the roadmap, a plain language AI layer, Indian languages, and WhatsApp intake.

13
00:02:29,255 --> 00:02:38,255
ClaimSaathi. Because every rejection must cite a clause, and now every family can read it. Try the live demo at the link on screen.
